        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">MAP 281 - Kanda/Col</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:19pt">
        <table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%">
          <tr>
            <td style="width:1.0%"/>
            <td style="width:98.900%"/>
            <td style="width:0.1%"/>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000;border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:middle">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:115%">Schedule Page: 358 Line No.: 6 Column: (d)</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Enterprise shared service costs are allocated to franchises via specific or general methods. Specific allocations are based on metrics that bear a reasonable correlation to the delivery of services, for instance some human resource services costs are allocated based on employee headcount. General allocations are based on "Modified Massachusetts" formula (MMF) which is determined by the proportion of three components: net revenues; gross property, plant and equipment; and gross payroll.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:19pt">
        <table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%">
          <tr>
            <td style="width:1.0%"/>
            <td style="width:98.900%"/>
            <td style="width:0.1%"/>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000;border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:middle">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:115%">Schedule Page: 358 Line No.: 12 Column: (d)</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Payroll and non-payroll charges for the benefit of the operating area that are not specific to a franchise are allocated to franchises in the operating area via specific or general methods. Specific allocations are based on metrics that bear a reasonable correlation to the delivery of services, for instance some human resource services costs are allocated based on employee headcount. General allocations are based on "Modified Massachusetts" formula (MMF) which is determined by the proportion of three components: net revenues; gross property, plant and equipment; and gross payroll.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:19pt">
        <table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%">
          <tr>
            <td style="width:1.0%"/>
            <td style="width:98.900%"/>
            <td style="width:0.1%"/>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000;border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:middle">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:115%">Schedule Page: 358 Line No.: 13 Column: (d)</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Employees' direct assignment payroll and non-payroll charges recorded to a specific work order for the benefit of the Transmission, Power &amp; Gulf Operating Area that are not specific to a franchise are allocated to franchises included in the operating area via general allocations based on "Modified Massachusetts" formula (MMF).</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:19pt">
        <table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%">
          <tr>
            <td style="width:1.0%"/>
            <td style="width:98.900%"/>
            <td style="width:0.1%"/>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000;border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:middle">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:115%">Schedule Page: 358 Line No.: 18 Column: (d)</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Salt Lake City, Utah building rent is allocated based on employee labor hours.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:19pt">
